course: dictionary
lesson: 3383
title: Exit: a way out, and to leave
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Exit is a word with two jobs. As a noun it is a door or way out: «Know where the nearest exit is at events.» As a verb it means to go out or leave, or to close a program.
explain: Context tells you which job the word is doing. In «He made a quick exit», exit is a noun meaning the act of leaving. In «exit the game», it is a verb meaning to close it down. Ask yourself: is this word a thing, or an action?
explain: Read «If a crowd starts pushing, move sideways towards the edge where there is space.» The clues are crowd, pushing and nearest exit. Exit must mean a way out, so you know where to go when a crowd gets dangerous.
fact: Exit (noun) means a door or way out of a building, room, vehicle or motorway.
fact: Exit (noun) can also mean the act of leaving, as in «He made a quick exit».
fact: Exit (verb) means to go out or leave, or to close a program on a computer.
fact: «Emergency exit» and «fire exit» are ways out that people use in an emergency.
fact: Exit signs are green in the UK but red in the USA.
exercise: In «Know where the nearest exit is at events», what is an exit? | *A way out of the building | A seat near the stage | A loud noise | A ticket for the show
exercise: «An exit poll asks some voters how they voted as they leave.» What does exit mean in this sentence? | A special kind of paper | To shout loudly | A way into a shop | *The act of leaving
exercise: Sam says, «I'll exit the game now.» What does exit mean here? | *To close it down and leave | To paint the screen | To build a castle | To buy a new game
test:
test: «The Baltic Sea is brackish, because its only exit is through narrow Danish straits.» In this sentence, exit means: | *A way out | A kind of fish | A type of salt | A fresh water river
test: In a play script, what does «Exit» tell the actor to do? | The audience claps | The lights go on | *The character leaves the stage | The character sings a song
exam: Which sentence uses exit as a verb? | *Please exit the program now | The exit was blocked | Find the exit sign | Her exit was quick
